{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"hub","type":"text","text":"CAT4 — Students invent process strategies when teaching is thin\nRQ2 · finding","x":140,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cases","type":"text","text":"Cases\nS1 S2 S3 S5","x":-220,"y":-80,"width":300,"height":70,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"memo_group","type":"text","text":"**Memos** (4) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S1M2]] — worked examples bridge text and diagram\n- [[S2M2]] — examples and professor check substitute for process\n- [[S3M2]] — professor feedback as correctness gate\n- [[S5M3]] — early sharing and self-initiated drafts replace waiting","x":-330,"y":206,"width":520,"height":192,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"code_group","type":"text","text":"**Codes** (13) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S1-C13]] — text-to-model via trial and error\n- [[S1-C15]] — no remembered step-by-step teaching\n- [[S1-C23]] — learn modelling best from worked examples\n- [[S2-C11]] — trial and error then ask professor\n- [[S2-C14]] — replicate reasoning from completed examples\n- [[S2-C15]] — start with objects then draw relationships\n- [[S2-C17]] — elements taught not explicit modelling process\n- [[S3-C07]] — waited for professor feedback to feel sure\n- [[S3-C13]] — picks first option when two seem valid\n- [[S3-C18]] — slides alone not enough without feedback\n- [[S5-C04]] — drafts version one without waiting for demo\n- [[S5-C07]] — small prototype settles modelling disagreements\n- [[S5-C14]] — wants weekly assessed diagram peer reviews","x":540,"y":206,"width":520,"height":444,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"explainer","type":"text","text":"What this means\n\nWhen the course does not spell out a process, students invent their own — trial and error, early drafts, turning symbols into words, and similar tactics.","x":80,"y":-360,"width":520,"height":150,"color":"1"}
	],
